<mxCell id="scheduler" value="SCHEDULER SERVICE&#10;&#10;Leader-elected&#10;60s look-ahead&#10;ZADD to Redis&#10;Failover &lt; 30s" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffcc80;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="195" width="200" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="workers" value="WORKER POOL&#10;&#10;ZPOPMIN atomic&#10;Execute jobs&#10;Heartbeat every 30s&#10;Update status&#10;N stateless pods" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#c8e6c9;strokeColor=#388e3c;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="850" y="195" width="200" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="monitor" value="MONITOR SERVICE&#10;&#10;Scan stuck jobs&#10;Check heartbeat TTL&#10;Re-enqueue failed&#10;30s polling" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1090" y="195" width="200" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="principles" value="KEY DESIGN RULES&#10;&#10;1. Redis ZPOPMIN atomic queue: Sorted set score = next_run_unix_timestamp. ZPOPMIN atomically pops lowest score (earliest due job). Multiple workers can't grab same job. Time-based priority built-in. NOT Kafka (FIFO, can't query 'all jobs due NOW').&#10;&#10;2. Leader-elected Scheduler prevents duplicate enqueue: Only ONE Scheduler instance enqueues jobs to Redis. Leader holds Redis key with 30s TTL, renews every 15s. If leader dies, new leader elected in &lt; 30s via SETNX. Without leader election, all Scheduler instances would enqueue same job → duplicates in queue.&#10;&#10;3. At-least-once execution with idempotency: Worker crash → Monitor detects via heartbeat expiry → re-enqueues job with NEW execution_id. Both workers may complete. Jobs must be idempotent (check 'already sent email for user 42 today?' before acting). Simpler than exactly-once (no distributed transactions needed).&#10;&#10;4. Heartbeat-based stuck job detection: Worker sets Redis key job_heartbeat:{jobId} = workerId EX 90 every 30s. Monitor scans for RUNNING jobs, checks Redis heartbeat. If expired (TTL gone) → worker died → mark FAILED → re-enqueue. Without heartbeat, stuck jobs hang forever silently.&#10;&#10;5. Thundering herd prevention with jitter: 10,000 jobs at midnight → all workers busy at once → downstream services overwhelmed. Solution: next_run = cron_time + hash(job_id) % 300s. Spreads 10K jobs over 5 minutes (33 jobs/sec). Deterministic (same job always same jitter).&#10;&#10;6. Exponential backoff retry: Retry delays: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s. Prevents retry storms when downstream service is down. After max_retries (default 3) → DEAD_LETTER status → alert human → no more auto-retry." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="350" y="420" width="940" height="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

